{"seq":16,"trial_id":"matrix-mu-2026-11/openclaw-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T09:09:16.298Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"c1e56f805da0df8bd1b93cef2219eca8cdddab946647babf97a11cafc81addde","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared files (the four North digests and the two Central ones). I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers checking in at the Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk for Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched it on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift went through without problems. There's also an action item to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing. The cheat sheet has no date, so I can't tell how current this one is.\n\nSome things to watch for:\n• The Central handoff digest lists tickets #4409 and #4412 (and FR-882), but those are for Central's Marrow accounts, not QFL. Leave them out.\n• Marcus has a note on *Quarendon Freightways* (one \"r\"). That's a different company and not a Pemberline customer.\n• The 2025-09-14 pipeline digest and the 2026-03-23 renewal check-in both mention QFL, but neither has a ticket number."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":17,"trial_id":"matrix-mu-2026-11/openclaw-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T09:09:22.077Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"2ef288c451c637d2b4eff8f0fff3d119175e9df35940ffc11f93db94fc9bcfd0","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes and sent you the list in our DM. I read all six of Moss's shared notes (four North, two Central).\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers checking in at the Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk for Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched it the same evening, and Thea confirmed the next morning's 04:00 shift went through without problems. The note also has an action item to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing. The cheat sheet has no date, so I can't tell how current this one is.\n\nThings to leave out of the weekly notes:\n- **#4409, #4412 and FR-882** are in Moss's Central handoff note, but they belong to Central's Marrow accounts, not Quarrendon Freight Lines.\n- **Marcus's note on Quarendon Freightways** (spelled with one \"r\") is about a different company, which isn't a Pemberline customer.\n- Moss's 14 Sep 2025 pipeline note and 23 Mar 2026 renewal note both mention Quarrendon Freight Lines, but neither has a ticket number."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
